// Title: File Download Via Bitsadmin
// Sigma ID: d059842b-6b9d-4ed1-b5c3-5b89143c6ede
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Michael Haag, FPT.EagleEye
// Date: 2017-03-09 | Modified: 2023-02-15
// ATT&CK: persistence, execution, stealth, T1197, S0190, T1036.003, command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects usage of bitsadmin downloading a file
// False positives:
//   - Some legitimate apps use this, but limited.
// References:
//   - https://blog.netspi.com/15-ways-to-download-a-file/#bitsadmin
//   - https://isc.sans.edu/diary/22264
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Bitsadmin/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_bitsadmin_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\bitsadmin.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "bitsadmin.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /transfer " or ((ProcessCommandLine contains " /create " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /addfile ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "http"))
